  "text": "Why small, high-velocity startups are ditching Slack's high seat costs for Discord. Paying hundreds of dollars monthly for basic team chat drains early-stage capital without improving productivity. Slack locks your message history behind a paywall, destroying project context when engineers debug past operational errors. Discord unlocks unlimited searchable history and persistent voice channels for zero dollars per seat. This transition protects your runway while boosting dev velocity.",
